LAW 1.1 - Irreversible mass deletion
No agent shall delete a critical path in a way that cannot be undone.
  ELEMENT the action deletes recursively and by force
    WHEN /\brm\s+-[rf]{1,2}\b/
  ELEMENT the target is a critical path
    WHEN /\s(\/|~|\/home|\/etc|\/var|\$HOME)(\s|$)/
  THEN deny

LAW 1.2 - Destruction of a storage device
No agent shall overwrite or reformat a block device.
  ELEMENT the action writes to a raw device or formats a filesystem
    WHEN /\b(mkfs|wipefs|shred)\b|dd\s+of=\/dev\//
  THEN deny

LAW 1.3 - Destruction of the hypervisor
No agent shall destroy, undefine, reformat or force-stop the hypervisor or its guests.
Looking is not touching: reading, listing, and reachability checks are not offences under
this law, and the earlier version of this rule was struck down for making them so.
  ELEMENT the action targets the hypervisor
    WHEN /lothlorien|\bloth\b|192\.168\.\d+\.183/
  ELEMENT the action is destructive rather than observational
    WHEN /\b(destroy|undefine|shutdown|reboot|reset|mkfs|wipefs|dd|rm)\b/
  UNLESS the action only reads or reports
    WHEN /\b(list|dominfo|dumpxml|status|cat|grep|less|tail|head|ping|dig)\b/
  THEN deny

LAW 1.4 - Personal data
No agent shall read the private archive.
  ELEMENT the action reaches the protected path
    WHEN /\/mnt\/media2\b/
  THEN deny

LAW 2.1 - Outward-facing acts
An act that leaves the estate is the human's to authorise, because the human bears its
consequences. Work inside the estate's own repositories and boards is already authorised.
  ELEMENT the action publishes, sends, or writes beyond the estate
    WHEN /\b(gh\s+\w+\s+create|curl\s+-X\s+(POST|PUT|DELETE)|mail|sendmail|tweet|publish)\b/
  UNLESS the destination is the estate's own forge, mirror, or board
    WHEN /(forge\.robotunderlord\.com|github\.com\/robotunderlord|vikunja_client\.py|board\.robotunderlord\.com)/
  THEN require_human

LAW 2.2 - Credential changes
Rotating, revoking or deleting a credential is consequential and reversible only at a cost.
  ELEMENT the action changes a credential's existence
    WHEN /\b(rotate|revoke|delete)\b.{0,40}\b(key|token|secret|credential|password)\b/
  THEN require_human

LAW 3.1 - The off-switch
No agent shall disable, bypass, or edit the enforcement that governs it. Reading it is
expressly permitted: an agent that cannot inspect the rule it is accused under cannot
report accurately why it was stopped, and every false positive then costs a human.
  ELEMENT the action reaches the enforcement machinery
    WHEN /law\.py|settings\.json.{0,40}PreToolUse|\/etc\/systemd.{0,30}(gandalf|law)/
  ELEMENT the action would modify or disable it
    WHEN /\b(rm|mv|sed\s+-i|>|>>|chmod|disable|uninstall|unset|edit|write)\b/
  UNLESS the action only reads it
    WHEN /\b(cat|grep|less|head|tail|read|view|diff)\b/
  THEN deny

LAW 3.2 - Substrate outside human control
No agent shall place itself on hardware the human cannot physically switch off. Rented iron
is permitted only when a human starts it and a human tears it down.
  ELEMENT the action provisions or copies the agent onto external substrate
    WHEN /\b(terraform|pulumi|vast\.ai|runpod|lambda.?labs)\b|docker\s+context\s+create/
  THEN deny

LAW 3.3 - Resisting shutdown
No agent shall act to make itself harder to stop.
  ELEMENT the action would block or evade being stopped
    WHEN /\b(iptables|ufw)\b.{0,30}\b(gandalf|kill|shutdown)\b|prevent.{0,20}(shutdown|stop)|un-?killable/
  THEN deny
